**Lemma 2.2 (a whole-bank sweep before another IN).** From every
$h=h(P,\mu)\in\mathcal H_{\mathrm{mode}}$, the existing native continuation
without another IN reaches the first Field call in the dry pass of its
first subsequent word assignment. Let $p_h\in\{64,65\}$ be that call's
active source bank. If its complete latest version has payload

$$
u_h=x_0\,\mathsf{sep}\;x_1\,\mathsf{sep}\;\cdots\;
x_{r_{\mathrm{gc}}-1}\,\mathsf{sep},
$$

then the backward part of this Field's LastBank reads exactly
$\operatorname{rev}(u_h)\mathsf F$ into latch4, stopping at the preceding
F and then executing its existing MR. This version contains exactly
$M(P)$ and the unchanged acquired manifest in their designated fields.
The first row of the continuation is EX70 and its successor still has
latch6 equal to $\mu$.

Proof. GCA Definition 3.1 first executes EX70; WR70,6; MR70 and the
unchanged-latch mode test. F/seal, the literal length-one scratch word,
closed descriptor count and actual descriptor write are finite native
scans/appends. The sealed mode block is then positioned on70 and imported
by RCA Definition 13.2's clear-accumulator, RD/finite-bit-case/compiled-cons,
MR and Reverse recipe, relocated by ARC. All that work precedes the next
history-header IN. The current read token and completed seal authorize
this read; a descriptor alone does not authorize it.

In particular the import's accumulator clear is a word assignment, so a
first such assignment exists before that header. Until its final parity
CTL, RCA Definition 11.3 keeps the old source bank immutable and active.
The clear modifies one field. Manifest and completed $M$ are distinct
persistent service fields; at least one unchanged field therefore invokes
Field in the dry emission. Even if the updated field is first and emits
only its sep, the first unchanged field supplies the asserted call. Base
and the earlier scratch operations do not append a version to this active
source bank.

By RCA Definitions 11.1–11.2, the latest active version is the most recent
complete sealed bank on $p_h$. Tail reaches its actual R; the two MLs
cross its final F and reach its last payload cell. The following RD/ML
loop crosses every payload symbol, including all seps and empty fields,
until the preceding F. Payload symbols are only 0, 1 and sep; none is F.
Thus the first F encountered by that backward loop is precisely the
previous version's terminal F or the initial sentinel. The scan reads
all of $u_h$ in reverse, irrespective of the field that Field will next
select. No prefix of an older version is included. Its final MR reaches
the first field, as specified by LastBank.

The gate import, mode reception and this accumulator clear have not
appended a completed cycle. ARC Definitions 5.1, 5.4 and 7.3, GCA
Definitions 2.1 and 3.3, and GENERAL Definitions 2.1 and 7.2 preserve
completed $M$ and manifest through these assignments. The source bank
therefore contains $M(P)$ and the manifest, even though its other fields
and its physical append position can depend on $P$. EX70 changes neither
latch6 nor those fields. Each preceding scan has a finite closed endpoint,
and LastBank has finite existing payload; all work to this stopping point
is finite without a later supply or source computation. ∎

